  "result": "`default_map` values for subcommands are now applied. The full test suite passes (1906 passed).\n\n**Cause:** in `Context.__init__` (`src/click/core.py:392`), a child context inherited the parent's whole `default_map`. It never looked up its own `info_name` entry, so the subcommand searched the top-level dict for `n` instead of `{\"sub\": {\"n\": 5}}`.\n\n**Fix:** the child context now takes `parent.default_map.get(info_name)`.\n\n**Check:** a group with a `sub` command and `default_map={\"sub\": {\"n\": 5}}` now prints `5` where it previously printed the option's own default of `1`.\n\nI didn't add a regression test, and nothing is committed.",
